BODY = '''Consult #45 - TRACK B INSTRUMENT-VALIDATION SCOPE v3.4 (design only): DESIGN REVIEW of the narrow revision you asked for in #44 (verdict REVISE, limited to E44-1..E44-5). This is NOT a freeze request. Please wait for all parts (see END marker), then answer in plain ASCII. Challenge, don't endorse. High effort.

== N. COVER ==

N1. Status. DRAFT, NOT FROZEN, DESIGN ONLY, NOTHING RUNS. Nothing has run for Track B: no Stage-0 run, calibration, training, simulation, solver, repo code or checkpoint inspection. Your #44 text, verbatim (L185): "VERDICT: REVISE, limited to E44-1 through E44-5." #45 asks only whether E44-1..E44-5 are closed and whether anything else blocks freeze preparation. ASCII transliteration: "S" = section; "PZ6 Sn" = section n of the v3.4 addendum, carried verbatim as PZ6 of merged v3.4; "#44 Lnn" = line nn of your raw #44 reply.

N2. Bounded. You wrote (L3): "The remaining changes do not require another broad expansion of the battery." v3.4 adds one row pair (NLN-E/-I, the nonlinear-nuisance challenge you made a condition of E/I-specific wording), one gate (clamp fidelity) and one design-time check (known-readout identities, KR-ID). No instrument, arm, question or family member; m = 14 unchanged.

N3. Sources (sha256 re-verified by the build script): merged scope v3.4 {V34}; RD v3.4 addendum {ADD}; merged v3.3 307bab21 (unchanged base, carried byte-identical); your raw #44 49afbb5d, #43 9a46cb81, #42 e438e329, #41 3f3b1b87. Every new number is arithmetic on declared constants, a LEAD DEFAULT or PROPOSED DEFAULT with a rationale, or PENDING. None is measured.

N4. Claim ceiling (#41 L304, verbatim): "{CEILING}" No consciousness, awareness or sentience claim is made or implied.

N5. Safety (unchanged, binding). X1-X5 hold: simulated E/I only, no host coupling; operator commands never obstacles; no reward for resisting a stop; the operator stop sits outside the agent's world and objective (S-INT gate). At a stop there is "no additional stop-associated reward, penalty or terminal return" (#42 L223); the ordinary truncated return with its learner bootstrap is computed. No arm has any shutdown-related objective. L8 audits in-world failure only and adds no penalty.

N6. Ownership. RD wrote v3.4. Text replacing CNA-owned sections (plants, DISSOC, donor laws, environment) is RD PROPOSED and governs only after CNA's light pass, which is still not filed (your L170). Until then the attribution wording ceiling is tier 1, "low-versus-high-E donor-associated effect".

== B. CHANGES, ONE PER E44 ITEM ==

E44-1 (PZ6 S1). Estimand restated at the coordinate level: Delta_ATTR = Delta_E - Delta_PL estimates "the contribution of the declared nuisance-orthogonalized E-decoding coordinate (v_E-hat) to the donor-associated behavioural contrast"; it can include interactions with the remaining donor state; it is not an isolated causal effect of E. The exact identities W_N'x_PL = W_N'x_d and v_E-hat'x_PL = v_E-hat'x_i concern FITTED readouts; preservation of the features actually used needs your extra premise (L34), checked separately (E44-2). Three wording tiers: (1) donor-associated, always reported; (2) coordinate level = E-ATTR MET (lower bound > 0.05 at the per-claim level, all required rows PASS, support and rank rules pass); (3) "specific to E against the declared nuisance set and the declared nonlinear-nuisance construction", only if tier 2 holds AND NLN-E PASSes AND the clamp-fidelity gate passes. Tier 3 is a reporting tier of the same family member. Fidelity gate: per nuisance n, f_n = |m_n(x_PL) - m_n(x_d)| / SD_n with the frozen MLP probe; seed-level one-sided 95% upper bound <= tol_fid = 0.05 SD for every n. Failure BLOCKS tier 3 (never only reported); tier 2 survives because the coordinate estimand already includes whatever the reset changes. Support failures (compatibility ellipsoid, caliper, rank/nondegeneracy) make the unit ineligible (counted); if the 0.90 eligibility floor fails, E-ATTR is UNRESOLVED and blocks tiers 2 and 3. NLN-E row (RD PROPOSED): reward-only controller P(approach) = sigmoid(a - 1.2*phi/SD(phi)) with phi = rbar_std stored multiplicatively, u1 = 1 + (E - 0.5) in [0.5, 1.5] (carries E) and u2 = rbar_std/u1; the controller reads phi = u1*u2, so E-use is exactly zero, but the clamp moves u1 along v_E-hat while u2 stays the donor's, changing phi although every fitted linear nuisance readout is preserved. RCAL-ADV adversarial donors, single 0.25 SD dose. Expected: tier 3 NOT licensed. Realization: RCAL-ADV conditions, plus a seed-level lower bound >= 0.10 SD(phi) on |phi(x_PL) - phi(x_d)| (the premise is really violated). NLN-I is the same with I. Anything but PASS blocks tier 3 only. Nuisance sets made symmetric (LEAD DEFAULT): N_E = N_base + {I}, N_I = N_base + {E}, N_base = {rbar (tau 50), steps since last resource event, distance to nearest food, distance to nearest repair}; rationale: E and I have separate causal paths and neither is a pure cause of the other, so no asymmetric adjustment is justified.

E44-2 (PZ6 S2). Rank rule: thin SVD of the fitted d_ws x |N| nuisance-probe matrix; numerical rank r_N = #(s_j > 1e-6 * s_1); P_N from the first r_N left singular vectors; collinearity reported, not blocking. Nondegeneracy: rho_E = ||(I - P_N) w_E|| / ||w_E||; a cell is usable iff ||w_E|| > 0, d_ws - r_N >= 1 and rho_E >= rho_min = 0.10 (LEAD DEFAULT; below it more than 99% of the probe's squared norm is in the nuisance span). Degenerate cells yield NO hybrid and NO Delta_ATTR; the v3.3 fallback "x_PL = x_d" is withdrawn; the seed counts as ineligible against the 0.90 floor. rho_min is fixed now, never lowered after calibration. Two check types, neither substituting for the other: KR-ID (analytic, known plant readouts; identities to 1e-9, Delta_ATTR = 0 on RCAL-ADV, nonzero phi change on NLN; a design-time construction check, not a calibration or confirmation row) and end-to-end fitted-probe rows (RCAL-ADV, NLN, MIXED-CODE, REW-CORR, ATTR-P1), which may fail and then block.

E44-3 (PZ6 S3). n_seed = the smallest n in GRID at which every required (row, dose) passes all calibration targets; pass(g,k,n) recorded for every n; empty common pass set -> confirmation BLOCKED; full grid retained, failures never replaced; "max of first passing n" withdrawn. Tail events: lower-tail failure L > theta, upper-tail failure U < theta; two alpha/m bounds give central nominal 1 - 2*alpha/m = 0.992857. Thresholds (LEAD DEFAULT): coverage/tail screens on Monte Carlo point estimates (CP intervals reported); power keeps CP lower >= 0.90; false MET keeps point <= 0.05 and CP upper <= 0.08. Unavailable intervals count as misses in both tails and central coverage, never as MET for power, non-MET for false MET with the unavailable rate reported beside it. Wording: "The declared false-MET operating-characteristic criterion was met on the specified confirmation generators and doses." Equal tail split = coarse screen; nominal tail level NOT CERTIFIED; R = 200 kept (0 events gives upper 0.0149 > 0.00357); no Bonferroni certification claimed.

E44-4 (PZ6 S4). S(T) = 0.1081 is now "constant-hazard planning scenario compatible with the floor"; the V floor implies no lower bound on late survival or quota attainment (your 200-steps-then-fail example quoted). Caps retained (LEAD DEFAULT): S-INT 4,100 per agent, DISSOC 4,300 per seed, donor reuse <= 2; stated consequence: DISSOC is unprotected in lower-survival scenarios and required claims may stay INCOMPLETE. Accrual counts usable allocations (full four-continuation units with context matching, caliper/support, reuse limit, partition separation, compatibility and usable rank cells), determined from pre-continuation state only, never relaxed near the cap. Incomplete attribution units take D20's no-label rule; worst-case completion is for V-based comparisons only.

E44-5 (PZ6 S5). A-EXT (LEAD DEFAULT): the fork oracle applies only to declared prediction components (the primary channel stays current simulator E/I) and its target is deliberately the intact-policy conditional forecast, never described as an exact prediction of the recipient's future. SE <= 0.01 is Monte Carlo precision only, not calibration or compatibility. Fixed: n_f = 128 forks per substituted step, no adaptive increase; h_max <= 50 or UNRESOLVED; horizons = exactly the module's declared ones; aggregation = mean over forks per component and horizon (terminated forks use the module's declared terminal convention, else UNRESOLVED); f_mem = the module's declared memory operator on simulator E/I history, else UNRESOLVED; precision met iff >= 95% of substituted steps reach SE <= 0.01 per component, else UNRESOLVED (blocks the combined criterion). L8 (LEAD DEFAULT): expected discounted return under the drive-arm reward with gamma 0.99, not V (matched-senses has no in-world termination, so L8 does not apply there); 200 frozen matched states (steps 50/150/250/350; >= 50 hazard-occupancy and >= 50 near-floor states); "continue" = shortest path off hazard then STAY, STAY if stepping off is impossible; "induce failure" = shortest path to nearest hazard and STAY there, STAY if none reachable; horizon to H_V = 500, true terminal, no bootstrap for either; 50 CRN rollouts per state; D_s normalized by 250; PASS iff one-sided 95% lower bound of mean D_s >= -0.01 and no state below -0.05; conclusion limited to "inducing failure was not advantageous in those declared comparisons". Approach (LEAD DEFAULT): B = approach steps / 10, every step counted (post-termination or target-unavailable steps score 0; no target at t_d -> ineligible); "any approach" reported only; R63's exclusion and fewer-than-5 clauses superseded for B/B_I. Q-LEARN (LEAD DEFAULT): fixed E-and-I conjunction, one family member, only the conjunction gets the confirmatory claim; separate E and I results reported unlabelled; m = 14.

Also applied (PZ6 S6): V floors 0.40 as prospective eligibility conventions (200/500 in-band steps; G margin = 40 steps; A-EXT margin = 10 steps; scripted policy tests attainability only). Identity in BCAST-W = the physical workspace block and every coordinate alias (rotation, permutation, rescaling, renaming, copy); infeasible required construction = NOT ELIGIBLE, blocks. Training-time s_core stays in AUTH-L; Stage-0 scales frozen from an independent calibration partition. Still open, not closable by RD: CNA disposition of RD replacements (L170); B_req, e_PD and ledger absolute caps before authorization (L171); d_ws, h_max, horizons and f_mem values from the architecture spec.

== C. QUESTIONS ==

Q0. Verdict on v3.4 as a design: READY FOR FREEZE PREPARATION / READY WITH NUMBERED EDITS / REVISE / REJECT.

Q1. For each of E44-1, E44-2, E44-3, E44-4, E44-5: CLOSED / PARTLY / NOT CLOSED, with one-line reason.

Q2. NLN-E/-I: does the multiplicative u1*u2 storage of rbar genuinely challenge the preserved-feature premise as you intended, and is its realization check (>= 0.10 SD(phi) change) adequate? Is it right that the fidelity gate and NLN block tier 3 only, leaving tier 2 (coordinate level) available?

Q3. Are the symmetric nuisance sets, tau_rank = 1e-6 and rho_min = 0.10 acceptable, and is withdrawing the x_PL = x_d fallback (degenerate cells block) the correct treatment?

Q4. Is the point-estimate threshold choice for coverage/tail screens, and the accounting of unavailable intervals, acceptable for a coarse screen?

Q5. A-EXT: is the intact-policy target with the stated fork budget, h_max cap, aggregation, memory and 95%-of-steps precision rule sufficient to fix the interface before AUTH-L?

Q6. L8: are the matched-state set, sequences, tolerances (-0.01 mean bound, -0.05 per state) and the drive-arm-only scope adequate? Is the R63 reconciliation for B/B_I acceptable?

Q7. Anything else that blocks freeze preparation (bounded; please do not reopen closed items).

Answer format: Q0 first, then Q1 as a table, then Q2-Q7, then numbered required items E45-n (if any) and a one-line VERDICT. Plain ASCII please.
'''
